pers  containing complex magical formulas and  diagrams  clearly zora is not just a magic knight  in the conventional sense he is also a  magical  mad scientist or i guess i should say  magical mad  alchemist and he clearly spends  incredible amounts of time  and effort crafting his spells  zora also wants to become the strongest  possible version of himself  and to do that he cannot rely on large  amounts of magic  either from himself or from nature as a  low-born commoner he has to rely on  creating complex magical formulas ahead  of time  he has to work harder than everyone else  but  interestingly enough this approach  actually has its advantages  if you work hard ahead of time and spend  a lot of time perfecting it  you can create an extremely complicated  spell without the need to use a lot of  mana  and it seems that because less magical  power is required to create such spells  they will not disappear as quickly as  stronger spells  so these spells can actually be more  durable  under the right conditions at least  that's my understanding of what  zora was trying to say here but in order  for magna to learn to use these new  complex spells  he needs to study hard and dedicate  himself diligently to this type of  training  since magna tends to be a brash and  impatient guy  zora has his doubts about whether magna  will be able to pull  this off however magna is utterly  determined to make this happen  and he throws himself wholeheartedly  into studying  and training eventually after  considering many different variables  including the compatibility of various  magic attributes  magna comes up with an insane new magic  formula  zora himself has never even thought of  something like this before  but although the concept isn't  impossible  zora tells magna that he will need  extraordinary time  and patience in order to actually  execute  this spell so magna decides to spend the  next  six months studying and preparing to  execute  this one magic spell all of his focus  goes into preparing and executing this  one spell  perfectly and as we know he finally  succeeds  in his shocking battle against dante i  mentioned this in my previous video but  this reminds me so much of kurapika from  hunter hunter  training for so long to use just one  specific spell  under very specific conditions and then  seeing all of that hard work pay off  is just so rewarding we see that dante's  magic power level is represented by the  number  1000 and magnus is represented by the  number  two this means that dante is literally  500 times  stronger than magna and so under normal  circumstances there is  absolutely no chance that magna could be  daunting  but thanks to soul chain death match  dante's magic power goes down to 501  and magna's magic power shoots up to 501  meaning that the two fighters are now  evenly matched  but since magna knew that this would  happen and he has been preparing for it  for half a year  he has a clear advantage magna has the  element of surprise  and dante will need some time to adapt  to what  just happened not only did dante's own  power shrink in half  but his opponent's powers suddenly  skyrocketed  that is not an easy situation to deal  with out of nowhere  and in the middle of a battle magna then  explains to dante that the chain which  is now connecting the two of them  is their soul itself so if dante tries  to destroy the chain he will be  destroying his  own soul this means that dante is stuck  fighting magna  under these specific conditions and he  can't just break free from the chain by  severing it through force magna then  continues to attack  dante and dante fights back the whole  thing turns into a bit of a magical  boxing match  with the two mages exchanging punches  dante tries to use his gravity magic to  take  magna out but because the two mages have  the exact  same amount of magic power magna is able  to withstand the attack without  losing his composure magna then  counter-attacks  and just s